  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00001",
      "text": "Indian comics artist, writer and illustrator Narayan Debnath was perhaps not known in the international arena but he is hailed as the father of Bengali language comic strips. His popular comic strips such as Handa Bhonda (1962), Bantul the Great (1965) and Nonte Phonte (1969) popularized Bengali comics and entertained Bengali speaking children and teens in India and Bangladesh for generations. On January 18, 2022, Debnath passed away at the age of 96 in a hospital in Kolkata after prolonged illness. His fans on social media are mourning this void in the world of Bengali comic strips.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 1,
      "body_start": 0,
      "body_end": 590,
      "source_links": [
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bantul_the_Great",
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bengali_language",
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Handa_Bhonda",
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narayan_Debnath",
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nonte_Phonte",
        "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/kolkata/narayan-debnath-dies-a-slice-of-childhood-lost/articleshow/88983492.cms",
        "https://twitter.com/DeadOverHeels_/status/1483397415743139841"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00002",
      "text": "Journalist Monideepa Banerjie from Kolkata thanked him:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 2,
      "body_start": 592,
      "body_end": 647,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00003",
      "text": "Entrepreneur Boria Majumdar remembers how Debnath's cartoon characters impacted his childhood:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 3,
      "body_start": 649,
      "body_end": 743,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00004",
      "text": "Researcher Swati Moitra also concurs:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 4,
      "body_start": 745,
      "body_end": 782,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00005",
      "text": "> Hulo = Cat",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 5,
      "body_start": 784,
      "body_end": 796,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "blockquote",
      "source_is_quotation": true
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00006",
      "text": "Debnath was born in 1925 in Shibpur, Howrah, near Kolkata, the capital of the Indian state of West Bengal. During the Second World War, he studied fine arts at the Indian Art College but did not finish his studies. He started his career by freelancing for advertising agencies creating logos. During the 1950s he illustrated several children's books, including adventure novels and translation of international classic books for a major publishing house Dev Sahitya Kutir.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 6,
      "body_start": 798,
      "body_end": 1270,
      "source_links": [
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kolkata",
        "https://www.anandabazar.com/west-bengal/narayan-debnath-the-legendary-bengali-comics-creator-passes-away-dgtl/cid/1324197"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00007",
      "text": "His legendary creations",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 7,
      "body_start": 1272,
      "body_end": 1295,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "h4",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00008",
      "text": "Handa Bhonda: His first comic strip Handa Bhonda started in 1962 in the Bengali children's monthly Shuktara, which is also published by Dev Sahitya Kutir. The story is about two young boys similar to the Laurel and Hardy characters. The skinny and mischievous Handa is always trying to get his bulky friend Bhonda in trouble, however, the humble Bhonda always emerges as the winner.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 8,
      "body_start": 1297,
      "body_end": 1679,
      "source_links": [
        "https://bn.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E0%A6%B6%E0%A7%81%E0%A6%95%E0%A6%A4%E0%A6%BE%E0%A6%B0%E0%A6%BE_(%E0%A6%AA%E0%A6%A4%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%B0%E0%A6%BF%E0%A6%95%E0%A6%BE)",
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Handa_Bhonda",
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laurel_and_Hardy"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00009",
      "text": "Handa Bhonda is the longest-running Bengali comic strip written by a solo writer-artist, and has been published for over five decades.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 9,
      "body_start": 1681,
      "body_end": 1815,
      "source_links": [
        "https://scroll.in/article/934297/meet-narayan-debnath-the-grandfather-of-bengali-comics-for-six-decades"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00010",
      "text": "Here is an animated episode from the series:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 10,
      "body_start": 1817,
      "body_end": 1861,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00011",
      "text": "https://youtu.be/xsS6y6V_LYA?t=13",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 11,
      "body_start": 1863,
      "body_end": 1896,
      "source_links": [
        "https://youtu.be/xsS6y6V_LYA?t=13"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00012",
      "text": "Bantul the Great: Bantul (Batul) is the first Bengali comic strip superhero defending people from robbers and hooligans since 1965, and it also appears in the magazine Shuktara. The big-bodied character with strong muscles was influenced by Debnath's friend, the famous Bengali bodybuilder Manohar Aich. But Bantul didn't have superpowers yet. During the Bangladesh liberation war and the India-Pakistan War of 1971, the editors and publishers requested Debnath to make Bantul invincible. The character had an insanely powerful physique and bullets would bounce off him ever since.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 12,
      "body_start": 1898,
      "body_end": 2479,
      "source_links": [
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bangladesh_War_of_Liberation",
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bantul_the_Great",
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indo-Pakistani_War_of_1971",
        "https://www.telegraphindia.com/west-bengal/how-bantul-was-born/cid/1009616"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00013",
      "text": "The series also runs on Indian television:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 13,
      "body_start": 2481,
      "body_end": 2523,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00014",
      "text": "Nonte Phonte: Nonte Phonte started to appear in children's monthly magazine Kishore Bharati in 1969. It is the fun-filled adventures of the two young boys Nonte and Fonte, who keep their boarding school superintendent on his toes.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 14,
      "body_start": 2525,
      "body_end": 2755,
      "source_links": [
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nonte_Phonte",
        "https://www.whatshot.in/kolkata/we-can-never-outgrow-these-5-bengali-comics-c-14691"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00015",
      "text": "Sandip Talukdar tried to translate a page from the Nonte and Fonte comics for international readers.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 15,
      "body_start": 2757,
      "body_end": 2857,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00016",
      "text": "Devarsi Ghosh at Indian news portal Scroll.in shares other less-known characters by Debnath:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 16,
      "body_start": 2859,
      "body_end": 2951,
      "source_links": [
        "https://scroll.in/article/934297/meet-narayan-debnath-the-grandfather-of-bengali-comics-for-six-decades"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00017",
      "text": "> Patalchand the Magician (created in 1969), a young neighbourhood magician whose powers solve local problems; Bahadur Beral (created in 1982), a wonder cat who is too smart for his own good; Danpite Khadu aar tar Chemical Dadu (created in 1983), a Rick and Morty-like pair of a young boy and his scientist grandfather whose weird inventions form the crux of the stories; and Petuk Master Batuklal (created in 1984), the last of Debnath’s serialised creations, who is a gluttonous schoolteacher devising ways to steal food but is always stopped in his tracks by the students.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 17,
      "body_start": 2953,
      "body_end": 3528,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "blockquote",
      "source_is_quotation": true
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00018",
      "text": "However, Twitter-user Vinod thinks that Debnath's most underrated character is Goyenda (detective) Kousik:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 18,
      "body_start": 3530,
      "body_end": 3636,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00019",
      "text": "Most of his comic series have been published as books, and some of his works were televised and ran for decades. The Indian Institute of Cartoonists paid tribute to the more than six decades of his comic strip career:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 19,
      "body_start": 3638,
      "body_end": 3855,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00020",
      "text": "Tributes on social media",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 20,
      "body_start": 3857,
      "body_end": 3881,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "h4",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00021",
      "text": "Many on Twitter shared their tributes with hashtags like #RIPNarayanDebnath and #BengaliComics.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 21,
      "body_start": 3883,
      "body_end": 3978,
      "source_links": [
        "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BengaliComics?src=hashtag_click",
        "https://twitter.com/search?q=%23RIPNarayanDebnath&src=typed_query"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00022",
      "text": "Writer Subharanjan shares an illustration of Debnath's cartoon characters:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 22,
      "body_start": 3980,
      "body_end": 4054,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00023",
      "text": "Journalist Soumyadipta Banerjee wonders whether the tradition of reading Bengali “comics” would continue:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 23,
      "body_start": 4056,
      "body_end": 4161,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00024",
      "text": "> Om Shanti is an invocation for peace or an invocation to God",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 24,
      "body_start": 4163,
      "body_end": 4225,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "blockquote",
      "source_is_quotation": true
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00025",
      "text": "Journalist Bihan Sen Gupta feels that the loss is personal:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 25,
      "body_start": 4227,
      "body_end": 4286,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00026",
      "text": "Debnath was also immensely popular in Bangladesh. Sports journalist Soumik remembers him:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 26,
      "body_start": 4288,
      "body_end": 4377,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00027",
      "text": "Writer and scientist A. M. (@bhalomanush) opines that Debnath never got the accolades he deserved:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 27,
      "body_start": 4379,
      "body_end": 4477,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00028",
      "text": "However, Debnath got some recognition in India. He received the Sahitya Akademi award in 2013 and also the Banga Bibhushan awarded by the Government of West Bengal, in the same year. He received an honorary D. Litt from Rabindra Bharati University in 2015.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 28,
      "body_start": 4479,
      "body_end": 4735,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.dnaindia.com/lifestyle/report-handa-bhonda-creator-narayan-debnath-gets-sahitya-akademi-award-a-look-at-the-life-and-works-of-the-comics-writer-1884322",
        "https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/narayan-debnath-creator-of-iconic-comic-characters-dies-at-97-101642532033487.html"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00029",
      "text": "Debnath was also awarded the Padma Sri, the fourth-highest civilian award of India in 2021, which he received in the hospital on January 13, 2022.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 29,
      "body_start": 4737,
      "body_end": 4883,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.ndtv.com/india-news/narayan-debnath-narayan-debnath-padma-shri-legendary-bengal-cartoonist-narayan-debnath-handed-over-padma-shri-medal-in-hospital-2707899"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-754771-b00030",
      "text": "Indian Twitter-user Shivani tweeted:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 30,
      "body_start": 4885,
      "body_end": 4921,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    }
  ],
